   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 19 of the laws of 1964, relating to incorporating the\nNesconset Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, and providing for\nits powers and duties, in relation to the purpose of such association and the\nuse of foreign fire insurance premium taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S7605",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7605-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1, 2, 3 & 7, Chap 19 of 1964",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7605\n\nSPONSOR: MATTERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 19 of the laws of 1964, relating to incorporat-\ning the Nesconset Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, and\nproviding for its powers and duties, in relation to the purpose of such\nassociation and the use of foreign fire insurance premium taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would amend chapter 19 of the laws of 1964 relating to incor-\nporating the Nesconset Firefighter's Benevolent Association in relation\nto its name, its management and control as well as the usage of money\nreceived from foreign fire insurance companies by the Association.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends sections 1,2,3 and 7 of chapter 19 of the laws of 1964\nrelating to the incorporating of the Nesconset Volunteer Exempt Fire-\nmen's Benevolent Association by changing the term \"Firemen's\" to Fire-\nfighter's\" in the name of the corporation. It also establishes member-\nship eligibility and purpose of the corporation as well as the usage of\nmoneys received from foreign fire insurance companies by the Associ-\nation.\n\nSection 2 of the bill establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to assist in the retention of volun-\nteer firefighters in the Nesconset community. Furthermore, it will\nprovide relief and assistance to volunteer members and their families\nwho are disabled, indigent or injured in the performance of their\nduties.\n\nSince the Nesconset Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association\nreceives Foreign Fire Insurance Premium Tax monies from the New York\nState Insurance Department and/or the Department of Financial Services,\nthe bill would allow them to use the funds in furtherance of all of the\nstatutory purposes.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
